Looking at the BarcodeHandler.java, I can see the issue. The code directly sets the user-provided value via `generator.setContent(value)` without any preprocessing for EAN and UPC barcodes. 

For EAN-13, the OkapiBarcode library expects 12 digits (it calculates the check digit automatically), but users are providing 13 digits (including the check digit). Similarly for UPC-A, it expects 11 digits.

Let me first create a test to confirm the issue, then fix it.

```bash
cat > /tmp/TestBarcode.java << 'EOF'
